+# Final review inv-2, cluster 24 (src-daemon)
+
+Source: base 60e287aadd08af10779df39e625200f28d4b7fa3, head 985d1eb6faaa2e92e4e01f430f0f2c07618bf6ad (both verified with `git rev-parse --verify`; review-source binding recorded by `bind-review-source`, exit 0). Caller checkout observed at HEAD 985d1eb, `git status --short` clean, before and after the review.
+
+Files: src/daemon/clone_status.rs, src/daemon/compose.rs, src/daemon/doctor.rs (slices 000137-000139). Spec: docs/superpowers/runs/2026-11-26-resurrect-seat-frictionless-restart/2026-11-26-resurrect-seat-frictionless-restart-design.md, including its Requirement baseline (B1-B4, no human scope changes) and the hg-lnw.25/.27 post-implementation notes. Bead hg-lnw.24 read for the graph-local reclassification rule.
+
+## Baseline trace through this cluster
+
+B1 (resurrect on undo). The cluster's part is the production adapter `LazyThreads::resurrect_seat` (compose.rs, lazy module) and the `clones.resurrect_held` status row plus the `resurrect held` doctor check. `resurrect_seat` takes the namespace guard, resolves the lazy `ServiceThreads` (now built with the host locator via `Endpoint::host`) and forwards to the real service; guard or locate failures map through `SeatRestoreOutcome::from_error`, where `Disconnected` becomes the retryable `Unreachable`. `resurrect_held` matches spec section 3: pending Restore with `threads_done: false`, refusal meta of the current epoch (`refused_meta` filters by epoch), fact `Retired{reversible: true}` on the Restore seat, and `now >= first_at + SEAT_LOST_AFTER` (90 s). It clears when the fact leaves reversible, the Restore is acknowledged or the epoch moves. The meta fields it reads (`first_at`, `pane`, `reason`) are written by `ThreadsExecutor::resurrect_seat` (src/threads/effects.rs) with `reason` serialized as the snake-case refusal. The production path from undo to the executor's call lies outside this cluster (seam reviewer's to trace).
+
+B2 and B4 (frictionless restart, U2 rebind). The cluster's part is `LazyThreads::rebind_held_seat` (same shape as resurrect), the `clones.restart_held` row and the `restart held` doctor check. `restart_held` matches spec 4.5: active seated clone, fact on the clone's seat reading `Unresolved` with `read_at >= incarnation:changed_at`, after the 90 s grace, reason from `rebind_refused_in` (incarnation-matched) else "rebind did not complete", remedy in the `human` form per the hg-lnw.27 note. Both rows are wired into production: `register_*` installs the `clones` status provider calling `clone_status_with_journal` -> `clone_status_at(.., Utc::now())`, and `doctor()` reads `comp("clones")` for both checks. Emission of the rebind effect and the keyless start gate are outside this cluster (seam reviewer).
+
+B3 (v4 via upstream 3.6.0). The cluster's part is the doctor upgrade step: `threads_check` adds "install herdr-threads >= 3.6.0 ..." when the disconnect reason carries the adapter's `level_refused` text (`service_session_v4`) or the `daemon_floor` text (`must be at least 3.6.0`). `Endpoint::locate` passes discovery's `ErrorKind::Unsupported` (the 3.6.0 floor refusal) through verbatim as `Disconnected`, so the threads probe's `error` carries the floor text the doctor matches. Pin and discovery code are other clusters.
+
+## Graph-local reclassification (hg-lnw.24)
+
+Every endpoint-raised failure in compose.rs (explicit config, namespace guard, namespace bind, host claim, intent dir, and the connection probe's `committed()` read) is now `Disconnected("graph-local: ...")` instead of `Rejected`. `from_error` maps that to `Unreachable` (retryable), so a resurrect or rebind hit by a local fault is retried in the same incarnation rather than recorded as a definitive refusal. Five fault-injection tests cover guard staleness, bind mismatch, host claim, broken intent dir and explicit-config error, each driving both restore calls through `LazyThreads`. The rewritten `seat_view_rejection_is_visible_in_threads_status_and_records_nothing` now uses a real socket stand-in that answers `SeatInspect` with threads' own `Unsupported`, which keeps `seat_view_error` meaningful only for threads-returned answers.
+
+Side effect, by design of the bead: the same reclassification applies to every other mutation through the lazy endpoint (invites, retirement, key reservation). A persistent local misconfiguration (explicit socket/instance configured inconsistently, committed namespace node differing from the discovered node) used to fail those effects as `Failed`; it now stays `Transient` and retries indefinitely. Operator visibility is preserved through the `threads` status component (`connected: false`, `error: graph-local: ...`) and doctor's `threads` line, because the connection probe goes through the same endpoint. Recorded below as Deferred OK.
+
+## Verification run
+
+In hg-build at head: `cargo test --lib daemon::` ran 81 tests, 80 passed; the one failure, `daemon::lock::tests::is_held_reports_holder`, is in an unchanged file and passed on an isolated rerun (`cargo test --lib daemon::lock`, 3/3), so it reads as load sensitivity rather than a cluster defect. `cargo test --lib restart_held` (6 passed) and `cargo test --lib resurrect_held` (5 passed). Leak check after each run: 0 processes under `/tmp/hg-*`.
+
+## Findings
+
+- restart_held emits rows for a seated clone whose bound pane no longer exists after a restart, so such a clone gets both a `resume_blocked` row and a `restart_held` row whose remedy names a dead pane (`--pane <gone pane>`, or `--pane unknown` when no binding is recorded); the rebind effect itself requires the pane to exist. Spec 4.5 does not exclude this case, so it is a usability wart, not a spec violation.
+- doctor's upgrade-step detection is a substring match on the disconnect reason (`service_session_v4`, `must be at least 3.6.0`); it is coupled to the adapter's message text, guarded only by the two doctor tests that build the messages from `level_refused` and `daemon_floor`.
+- Graph-local failures are now indefinitely retried as transient for all lazy-endpoint mutations, not only restore calls (see the reclassification section); visibility remains via threads status and doctor.
+
+## Verdict
+ready
+
+## Must fix before landing
+- none
+
+## Untested scope
+- No test drives the `restart_held` row in production conditions where threads is unreachable after a restart: no fresh seat read lands, so the row cannot appear (it requires `read_at >= changed_at`); the fake-tier "never attempted" test keeps the seat view reachable while mutations fail.
+- The `Endpoint::locate` passthrough of discovery's `ErrorKind::Unsupported` (daemon below 3.6.0) into the threads status `error` is not tested end-to-end through the doctor in this cluster; the doctor tests construct the message directly from `daemon_floor`.
+- Unit `daemon::lock::tests::is_held_reports_holder` failed once under the parallel `daemon::` run and passed in isolation; unchanged file, not investigated further.
+
+## Deferred OK
+- restart_held could skip clones whose bound pane is gone (already covered by `resume_blocked`) to avoid a remedy naming a dead pane.
+- Persistent graph-local misconfiguration now retries non-restore threads effects indefinitely instead of failing them; acceptable under hg-lnw.24 because threads status and doctor still surface it, but a needs-human escalation for a long-lived local fault may be worth a follow-up.
+- Doctor upgrade-step detection relies on adapter message substrings; a typed reason in the threads status component would be sturdier.
